message: "If you use this software, please cite the software and version. Version 1.0.0 is currently a release candidate, not a published release."
type: software
title: "Reproducible Retrieval Evaluation: A Workbench for Lexical, Semantic, and Hybrid Search"
version: 1.0.0
authors:
  - given-names: Nathan John
    family-names: Chandrasekar
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-9702-8164"
repository-code: "https://github.com/vera-rubin/retrieval-evaluation-workbench"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - information retrieval
  - reproducibility
  - lexical search
  - semantic search
  - hybrid search
  - research software
abstract: >-
  I present a standalone evaluation workbench for lexical, semantic, and hybrid
  retrieval over a fixed synthetic corpus. It compares SQLite FTS5 BM25,
  BGE-small-en-v1.5, all-MiniLM-L6-v2, and two reciprocal-rank-fusion combinations.
  The software includes 300 synthetic records, 188 explicitly labeled queries,
  scope and status eligibility, exact full-record checks, result-contract tests,
  supplied-trace checking, compatible-run comparison, and static reports. Pinned
  model revisions and dependencies support local CPU reproduction on the tested
  Windows CPython 3.13 x64 platform. An accompanying technical report documents
  methods, measured re-evaluation, and limitations. The known historical query
  split is re-evaluated without retuning; it is not a newly blinded experiment.
  The fixtures and labels are model-authored synthetic examples, not a
  human-validated benchmark. This is software with an accompanying report,
  not a peer-reviewed journal publication.

  AI use: OpenAI Codex assisted software development, synthetic-fixture and label
  generation, analysis, review, visualization code, and manuscript preparation;
  ChatGPT supported earlier planning. I retain responsibility for the approved
  published content.
